  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Win the ball back in the middle third",
  "description": "A 7v7 game with goalkeepers on a 7v7 pitch. All outfield players stay in the middle third, which is marked with cones on the touchlines.\n\nBlue always starts with the ball from their goalkeeper and must keep it within the team in the middle third. Red tries to win it. Once red has won the ball they need five passes within the team in the middle third – then they may leave the zone and attack blue's goal. Blue must win the ball back before red gets there.\n\nSwap roles after a few attacks. Harder for red: blue may defend over the whole pitch even after red has left the zone, and red may counter straight after winning the ball with no passes needed. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "When you lose the ball: press right where the ball is before the opponents can turn."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Stay close to each other when you have the ball – then you are already close when it is lost."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "The goalkeeper moves up and reads long balls in behind when the team loses the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Red: play the first pass after winning the ball away from pressure, and create space between players."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "difficulty": 3,
